course: dictionary
lesson: 11588
title: Opposite sides of the world
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Antipodes is a word about places on opposite sides of the Earth. Two places are antipodes when they are exactly opposite each other, with the Earth in between. «My cousin lives in Auckland, which feels like the other end of the world from our home.» The clue is "other end of the world", which points to the idea of opposite places.
explain: Antipodes is a plural noun, so it often comes with "the", as in «the Antipodes». In Britain, people use the Antipodes as a name for Australia and New Zealand, because they lie on the far side of the world from Britain. «Our class is learning about the Antipodes this term.»
explain: The adjective is antipodean, as in «an antipodean summer», which means a summer in the far-away part of the world. Be careful not to mix the word up with antipathy, which means a strong dislike. Alice in Wonderland does this when she falls down the rabbit hole and wonders if she will land among the antipathies.
fact: Antipodes means places that are exactly opposite each other on the Earth.
fact: «If you dug a tunnel straight through the centre of the Earth, you would come out at your antipode.»
fact: For most places in Europe, the antipode is in the ocean, near New Zealand.
fact: In Britain, «the Antipodes» is a name for Australia and New Zealand.
fact: «Antipathy» means a strong dislike. It is a different word, so do not mix the two up.
exercise: If you dug straight through the centre of the Earth from your home, where would you come out? | Your nearest school | The same spot where you started | *The antipode, the spot exactly opposite you on the Earth | A place on the Moon
exercise: In Britain, «the Antipodes» usually means which two countries? | France and Spain | Canada and Japan | *Australia and New Zealand | Scotland and Wales
exercise: «Antipathy» sounds like antipodes. What does antipathy mean? | A type of ocean | *A strong dislike | A happy feeling | A place on the far side of the world
test: Which two countries do people in Britain often mean by «the Antipodes»? | Brazil and Argentina | Ireland and Iceland | *Australia and New Zealand | Egypt and India
test: Which part of speech is antipodean? | Noun | Verb | Adverb | *Adjective
exam: Alice wonders if she will land among the antipathies. Why is this a mix-up? | Both words mean the same thing | *Antipathies means dislikes, but antipodes means places on opposite sides of the Earth | Antipathies is a kind of dinosaur | Antipodes means dislikes
